  "notes": "⛔ `low` because the research marks this entry medium-low and says the construction is consistent but the production documentation is limited [LOW-CONF]. The numbers below are a reading of a consistent catalog, not sourced measurements. Two things the research is specific about carry the file. First, restraint: \"restrained kick syncopation\", \"soft, roomy claps\", \"light triplet fills\", \"low distortion\" — so this is the softest kit in the batch, with `velocityTiers` pulled down, the batch's lowest `snareRoll.rampJitter` at 5 and its narrowest velocity ramp, a widened `layerClapOffsetMs` for the room, and `bass808.distortion` at `none`. Second, dorian: the research names minor AND dorian with R&B extensions, so `scales` weights them equally and `extensions` runs 7ths at 0.5 with `susSubstitutionProb` 0.25. The harmonized hook stacks are the counter's paired styles at `densityRatio` 0.5. ⚠ The INFERRED parameter is the whole drum row — \"restrained\" and \"light\" are adjectives, and the numbers that implement them here are inference. The chord families (i–VI–III–VII and i–iv–VII) are the researched part of this file and are the part to trust. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
